SUMMARY:National Public Lands Day
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Saturday\, September 26\, for National Public Lands Day\, the nation’s largest single-day volunteer event for public lands! This is your chance to give back to Hermann Park\, one of Houston’s most cherished green spaces. \nWhether you’re pulling invasive weeds\, planting native grasses or helping with trail maintenance\, your time and energy will directly support the health and beauty of the park for generations to come. \nAll ages welcome – no experience necessary! Bring your friends\, family\, or coworkers and help us make a lasting impact. \nSign up for a session at McGovern Centennial Gardens\, the Commons\, or the Heart of the Park HERE.
URL:https://hermannpark.org/event/national-public-lands-day/
LOCATION:McGovern Centennial Gardens\, 1500 Hermann Drive\, Houston\, TX\, 77004\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://hermannpark.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/mcg_mount4-e1757000165605.jpg
END:VEVENT
