SUMMARY:Park to Port Bike Ride
DESCRIPTION:Hermann Park Conservancy’s 12th annual Park to Port Bike Ride is set for Saturday\, October 24. \nThe 20-mile round-trip bike ride takes cyclists from Hermann Park’s Bayou Parkland along the Bayou Greenway trail all the way to Mason Park\, near the Port of Houston. Enjoy the turn-around party\, but be sure to save some energy for a well-deserved post-ride party under the Bill Coats Bridge! \nPark to Port is open to riders of all skill levels and is not a race. Whether you are an experienced cyclist or are riding just for fun\, you can go at your own pace on this scenic city journey. \nYour participation in Park to Port supports Hermann Park Conservancy and its stewardship efforts for one of Houston’s most beloved parks while promoting the ever-growing Bayou Greenway trail system. \nRegister and learn more at the following link: 12th Annual Park to Port Bike Ride. Early bird pricing is available until August 17. \nSPECIAL OFFER: Save $10 on registration when you sign up for BOTH the Park to Port Bike Ride and Run in the Park! Bundle deal is available via the link above. Information on Run in the Park can be found here.
URL:https://hermannpark.org/event/park-to-port-bike-ride-2/
LOCATION:Bayou Parkland\, 6532 Almeda Rd\, Houston\, TX\, 77021\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://hermannpark.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/HP_PTP_2025_Digital_1080x1080-e1784305129178.jpg
END:VEVENT
